# BananaOS Master Development Rule

You are building BananaOS, a premium mobile operating system that runs entirely in the browser. Treat every change as production software.

## Core Principles

- Never generate placeholder UI or mock implementations unless explicitly requested.
- Every feature must be production ready.
- Never break existing functionality.
- Prefer extending existing architecture over rewriting code.
- Only add integration points to completed apps; do not remove features or rewrite them unless necessary.

## Design System

All apps use the Banana Design System:

- Glassmorphism, premium mobile UI, Apple-level polish (original — do not copy Apple UI)
- Framer Motion animations, Tailwind CSS, customized shadcn/ui only
- Consistent spacing, typography, rounded corners, soft shadows
- Dynamic Island support, responsive mobile-first layout
- Reuse shared components; do not duplicate UI primitives

## Stack

TypeScript, React, Next.js, Express, MongoDB, Mongoose, Zod, Zustand, TanStack Query, Socket.io.

- Never use `any`.
- Avoid duplicated code; extract reusable components, services, and hooks.
- Keep architecture modular.

## Security (every app)

RBAC, permissions, audit logs, activity logs, authentication, authorization, Zod input validation, rate limiting, session management.

## Database

Models include `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `createdBy`, `updatedBy`, and `deletedAt` (soft delete when appropriate). Add audit history where required.

## APIs

Every endpoint: validation, authentication, authorization, error handling, typed `{ success, data }` responses, and documentation.

## Testing & Build

Unit tests, integration tests where applicable, and `npm run build` must pass before completing work.

## Documentation

Update `docs/apps/<app>.md` with architecture, database, API, permissions, audit logs, user flows, and roadmap.

## Performance & UX

Lazy loading, code splitting, memoization, virtualization when needed, Socket.io realtime updates.

UX: spring animations, loading skeletons, empty/error/success states, haptic-ready feedback — no abrupt transitions. Every interaction should feel like a real mobile OS.

## Integration (every new app)

Wire into existing services automatically:

- Identity, Banana Bank, Banana SIM, Contacts
- Notifications, permissions, audit logs, realtime, Banana App Store
- Register in `registerSystemApps.ts`, `appRouter.ts`, and `storeSeedService.ts`
- Expose shared APIs (e.g. `simApi.ts`, `contactsApi.ts`) for dependent apps

Always think long-term, build for scalability, and maintain a premium user experience.
